# Archon environment for the Conduit Playwright + TypeScript project.
# Copy to .archon/.env for Archon-only variables (never commit secrets).
# Test settings (BASE_URL, HEADLESS, TEST_USER_*, ...) stay in the project .env — see .env.example.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PROJECT
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Absolute path of this project's main checkout. Archon loads .archon/.env into every workflow node, and workflows
# run in an isolated git worktree: the first bash node (.archon/scripts/workspace-setup.sh) links node_modules and
# copies .env, .auth and .archon/.env from PROJECT_PATH into the worktree, which has only the tracked files. Bash
# nodes themselves stay in the worktree, not in PROJECT_PATH. When it is unset the main checkout is read from git.
#   archon workflow run playwright-tests-execution --cwd /Users/vitalyshadrin/Projects/interview/conduit-realworld "tests/ui/auth.ui.spec.ts"
PROJECT_PATH=/Users/vitalyshadrin/Projects/interview/conduit-realworld

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MODEL LEVELS (documented here; edited in .archon/config.yaml)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Archon does not read models from .env — change aliases in .archon/config.yaml.
# Workflow AI nodes reference these as model: '@implementer' etc.
#
#   @planner      → opus   / effort high    (plan)
#   @implementer  → opus   / effort high    (implement / typecheck-lint fix / verify / heal locators)
#   @reviewer     → opus   / effort medium  (conventions review / test design review)
#   @general      → haiku  / effort low     (triage / reports)
#
